United Robots is a technology company developing autonomous mobile robots for industrial facilities, warehouses, and logistics centres. We create complete solutions encompassing electronics, control systems, autonomous navigation, sensor integration, robot software, and a cloud platform for managing fleets of devices.

We are looking for a versatile Robotics Software Engineer who will participate in designing, developing, integrating, and testing software for autonomous mobile robots. We need someone who can view a robot as a complete system and move confidently between software, sensors, electronics, and the device’s real-world behaviour.

Responsibilities



- Developing software for autonomous mobile robots;
- Designing, implementing, and maintaining components operating in ROS and ROS 2 environments;
- Developing software in C++ and Python;
- Integrating sensors, actuators, motor controllers, onboard computers, and other robot components;
- Developing communication modules and interfaces between individual subsystems;
- Implementing and integrating algorithms for localisation, navigation, motion planning, and mission execution;
- Integrating data from LiDARs, cameras, ToF sensors, encoders, IMUs, and other sensors;
- Developing control logic for the robot’s working and actuating components;
- Implementing status reporting, diagnostics, telemetry, and data-logging mechanisms;
- Diagnosing problems encountered during testing, deployment, and robot operation at customer sites;
- Analysing logs and data recorded during real-world device operation;
- Creating unit, integration, and system tests;
- Participating in simulation tests and tests conducted on physical robots;
- Optimising software performance, stability, and reliability;
- Collaborating with teams responsible for mechanics, electronics, embedded systems, backend services, and the cloud platform;
- Preparing technical documentation and instructions for developed components;
- Participating in code reviews and ensuring compliance with software development standards;
- Supporting robot commissioning, acceptance testing, and deployment at customer locations.

Key objectives of the role



- Developing stable and scalable software for autonomous robots;
- Increasing the reliability of robots operating in real industrial environments;
- Developing a modular architecture that enables common components to be used across different robot types;
- Reducing the time required to integrate new sensors, devices, and functionalities;
- Improving issue diagnosis and analysis of robot behaviour;
- Ensuring seamless cooperation between robot software, embedded systems, and the cloud platform;
- Contributing to the migration and development of ROS 2-based solutions;
- Preparing software for deployment across a growing robot fleet.

Requirements



- A minimum of 2 years of relevant professional experience;
- Experience developing software for robots, autonomous systems, embedded devices, or real-time systems;
- Practical knowledge of ROS or ROS 2;
- Good knowledge of C++ and/or Python;
- Very good knowledge of Linux;
- Knowledge of Git and collaborative software development practices;
- Ability to design and develop modular software;
- Knowledge of inter-process communication and distributed system architectures;
- Experience integrating hardware and software;
- Ability to diagnose issues using logs, telemetry, and observed device behaviour;
- Basic knowledge of communication protocols used in robotics, such as CAN, Ethernet, TCP/IP, UART, RS-232, or RS-485;
- Understanding of the operating principles of sensors used in robotics;
- Ability to solve technical problems independently;
- Willingness to test software on physical robots;
- Ability to collaborate with multidisciplinary teams;
- English proficiency sufficient to work confidently with technical documentation and communicate effectively in day-to-day work.

